      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Manually setting a low stock level to force a conversion spike carries significant operational risk if the true inventory is much higher. While the short-term margin gain might look appealing, it jeopardizes customer trust and could lead to negative reviews or fulfillment issues if customers expect a sell-out that doesn't occur. A more sustainable strategy would be to increase urgency through high-quality marketing copy that highlights the product's desirability, rather than fabricating the inventory count.",
